  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior to occupation of the development hereby permitted, a Statement of Conformity\rshall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Statement\rof Conformity will be signed by a suitably qualified ecologist named within the Biodiversity\rEnhancement and Management Plan (BEMP) and include evidence in the form of full details\ron:\ra) time stamped photographs of each habitat undergoing creation or enhancement\rb) post completion photographs of each habitat / enhancement\rc) post installation photographs of each nesting / roosting feature under Condition 2\rThis condition is to certify that the details for each habitat / feature, as approved under the\rBEMP, are in accord with the submitted information.\r\rReason: To enhance the biodiversity value of the land in accordance with Policy 26 of the\rSutton Local Plan 2018",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with the approved\rEnergy Statement PO2 (Ref: 510549-ELE-BL-XX-RP-YE-51001) prepared by Elementa\rConsulting Ltd and dated 9 February 2022 and the Mechanical Equipment Schedule\r(Ref: 510549) prepared in January 2022. Prior to first occupation, written confirmation that\rthe approved renewable energy measures have been implemented together with 'as-built'\rStandard Assessment Procedure (SAP) outputs demonstrating that each of the dwellings\rhas achieved the targeted reduction in CO2 emissions must be submitted to the Local\rPlanning Authority and approved in writing. All of the approved measures must thereafter be\rretained for as long as the development is in existence.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with the approved\rTM59 Overheating Report PO2 (Ref: 510549-ELE-BL-XX-RP-YE-51002) prepared by\rElementa Consulting Ltd and dated 9 February 2022. Prior to first occupation, written\rconfirmation that each of the approved cooling measures and specifications must be\rsubmitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing. All of the approved\rmeasures must thereafter be retained for as long as the development is in existence.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018"
  ],
